 "script": [
  {
   "id": "hook",
   "text": "A hurricane has crawled along Mexico's coast for days. Is the worst still ahead?"
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "text": "Hurricane Simon is creeping northwest at about three miles per hour, its eye offshore, the hurricane center said. Outer bands still hit towns near Puerto Vallarta, where the airport reopened to commercial flights Tuesday, its operator said."
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "text": "Mexican officials reported five deaths from storms this week. Four were in Baja California, from the remnants of storm Rachel. One was in Guerrero, where a wall collapsed. Forecasters expect five to ten inches of rain along the coast, and up to fifteen in Sinaloa by Thursday."
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "text": "Is the worst over? The hurricane center says some weakening is likely, and Reuters reports forecasters still warn of life-threatening flooding and mudslides. But Simon should stay a hurricane through midweek, and could strengthen again by Wednesday."
  },
  {
   "id": "cta",
   "text": "Will Simon come ashore in Mexico this week? Yes or no?"
  }
 ],
